  "Number": 10,
  "Question": "The lines \\(L\\) and \\(K\\) are symmetric to each other with respect to the line \\(y=x.\\) If the equation of line \\(L\\) is \\(y=ax+b\\) with \\(a\\ne0\\) and \\(b\\ne0,\\) then the equation of \\(K\\) is \\(y=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac1a x+b\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\frac1a x+b\\)",
    "C": "\\(-\\frac1a x-\\frac ba\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac1a x+\\frac ba\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\frac1a x-\\frac ba\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Reflection across \\(y=x\\) interchanges a point's coordinates. Thus \\((x,y)\\) lies on \\(K\\) exactly when its reflection \\((y,x)\\) lies on \\(L\\).\n\nSubstituting \\((y,x)\\) into the equation of \\(L\\) gives\n\\[\nx=ay+b.\n\\]\nSince \\(a\\ne0\\), subtracting \\(b\\) and dividing by \\(a\\) gives\n\\[\ny=\\frac{x-b}{a}=\\frac1a x-\\frac ba.\n\\]\nTherefore the answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
